---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';

const updated = 'August 2026';
const supportEmail = 'yash@typethink.ai';
---

<AppLayout
	title="Terms of Service — doodlebooth.lol"
	description="The terms for using doodlebooth.lol, a public wall where anyone can post a doodle."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
			<h1>Terms of <span class="grad">Service</span></h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Plain language, no tricks. doodlebooth.lol is a for-fun drawing wall — these terms
				explain what that means for you.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>

			<h2>What this site is</h2>
			<p>
				doodlebooth.lol is an entertainment project. It shows a public wall of doodles drawn by
				visitors. It is <strong>a novelty side project</strong> and nothing more.
			</p>

			<h2>No account needed</h2>
			<p>
				There is no sign up, no login and no password. Anyone can draw a doodle and drop it on
				the wall. Because of that, what appears on the wall is submitted anonymously by whoever
				drew it.
			</p>

			<h2>It's free</h2>
			<p>
				Using doodlebooth.lol costs nothing. There are no payments, no subscriptions, and no
				prizes or rewards attached to anything you post — you are drawing for fun and nothing
				else.
			</p>

			<h2>Your doodles</h2>
			<p>
				You keep whatever rights you have in what you draw. By dropping a doodle on the wall you
				give us permission to store it and display it publicly on the site. Don't submit anything
				you don't have the right to share.
			</p>

			<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>Keep it your own.</b> Don't upload art or images you don't have the right to post.</li>
				<li><b>No harassment.</b> Don't use the wall to target, shame or pile on a person.</li>
				<li><b>No automation.</b> Don't script, scrape or flood the submit endpoint.</li>
				<li><b>No illegal or harmful content.</b> Don't use the site for anything unlawful, hateful, or explicit.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We can remove any doodle and block any traffic at our discretion, without notice.
			</p>

			<h2>Getting removed</h2>
			<p>
				If a doodle on the wall shouldn't be there — including one you posted — email
				<a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> and we will remove it. You do not
				have to explain why.
			</p>

			<h2>No warranty</h2>
			<p>
				The site is provided as is. There is no guarantee it stays online, keeps your doodle, or
				preserves the wall.
			</p>

			<h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
			<p>
				To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising from your use of
				the site. This is a joke drawing wall — please treat it as one.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				These terms may change. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the
				updated version.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions, removals or complaints:
				<a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Back to the wall</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />
</AppLayout>
